course: dictionary
lesson: 12181
title: Happening at the same time
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words tell you about time. Concurrently is a formal word that means at the same time as something else. «The two trains ran concurrently along the same line.» Both trains moved during the same stretch of time, so the word tells you they overlapped.
explain: Look for the clue that two things happen together. «Maya practised the piano and the violin concurrently» means she played both at once, not one after the other. If you swap in "at the same time" and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The word also appears in law and in maths. «The two sentences run concurrently» means the person serves both at the same time, not one after the other. When two jobs run concurrently in a maths or science problem, their times overlap instead of adding up.
fact: Concurrently is an adverb, so it tells you how things happen. The adjective is concurrent.
fact: «Concurrently» means at the same time as something else.
fact: «Concurrent» is the adjective: «two concurrent events» are events that happen at the same time.
fact: In computing, programs that run concurrently do several jobs at once.
fact: A good check is to swap in "at the same time" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The two bands played concurrently on different stages.» What does concurrently mean? | Very loudly | *At the same time | One after the other | In a quiet room
exercise: Lena's two jobs run concurrently, so their times overlap. What does overlap suggest? | The jobs are both very short | The jobs take turns, one at a time | Nothing is happening at all | *Parts of the time are shared
exercise: «The two concurrent events took place on the same afternoon.» What does concurrent describe? | Events that only happen in the morning | *Events happening at the same time | Events that finished early | Events with no people present
test: «The lights in the hall and the kitchen were on concurrently.» In this sentence, concurrently means | slowly, one light at a time | *at the same time | a long way apart | in the dark
test: In a court case, sentences that run concurrently are | *served at the same time | paid off with money | served one after the other | cancelled completely
exam: Which word means the same as concurrently? | slowly | yesterday | underneath | *at the same time
